\begin_layout Enumerate
For a system with a single server (such as the 
\begin_inset Formula $M/M/1$
\end_inset

 and 
\begin_inset Formula $M/M/1/m$
\end_inset

 queue) the utilisation factor, 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho$
\end_inset

, is the probability that the queue state is not zero.
 For a lossless system we saw, using Little's formula (which is valid for
 
\begin_inset Formula $M/G/1$
\end_inset

 queues), that the utilisation factor is given by 
\begin_inset Formula $\rho=\frac{\lambda}{\mu}$
\end_inset

.
 Use the stationary distribution for the 
\begin_inset Formula $M/M/1/m$
\end_inset

 queue to compute the utilisation factor for the 
\begin_inset Formula $M/M/1/m$
\end_inset

 queue.
 Explain why it is not 
\begin_inset Formula $\frac{\lambda}{\mu}$
\end_inset

.
